cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite as below."
title: "ARS — Arithmetic Resonance Spectrograph"
abstract: >
  A calibrated multi-scale random-matrix-theory readout for arbitrary time
  series. Embeds a sequence into a chirp signal, runs a GPU-parallel bank
  of Farey-rational phase-locked loops against it, and extracts passage-time
  spacings that are unfolded and compared against random matrix theory
  predictions (Wigner GOE / GUE / Poisson). Validated against the Riemann
  ζ zeros and the Katz–Sarnak family symmetry of elliptic curve L-functions.
  The repository also contains llmspec/, "Shapes of LLM weights over
  training": a pre-registered study of language-model weight spectra across
  training (Pythia 70M–1.4B with PolyPythias seeds, OLMo 2 1B), with five
  own 70M training runs comparing learning-rate warmups and AdamW vs Muon
  (Arm B). It also contains specarith/, a spectral–arithmetic programme;
  its Phase 6 is a pre-registered, sealed prime-spectroscopy instrument
  (exact explicit-formula and Selberg trace-formula identities on the
  Riemann zeros, the zeros of L(s, χ₋₄) and the Maass spectrum of PSL(2,ℤ),
  with random-matrix nulls and picket-fence confusables), whose calibration
  gates all pass (specarith/ph6/PH6_FINDINGS.md). The calibrated instrument
  then read every testable published xp-type model (Sierra–Rodríguez-Laguna,
  Berry–Keating 2011, Sierra–Townsend; specarith/ph6/PH6_1_FINDINGS.md):
  each reproduces its own paper's counting constant and each fails the primes
  (no line at any log p^k, no spurious line), being locally an integrable
  crystal. specarith Phase 2 tests the Bogomolny et al. finite-size law on
  Odlyzko and Platt zeros: at heights 1e5–3e10 the O(N^-2)-truncated law
  under-describes the spacing distribution at 0.5–1% precision
  (specarith/ph2/PH2_FINDINGS.md). Its second part (seal PH2R2_SEAL_1.0)
  measures the amplitude of the Conrey–Snaith (Bogomolny–Keating)
  arithmetic lower-order term in the zeros' pair correlation at five fresh
  heights 7e6–2e10: full strength in every bin, pooled 1.003 ± 0.006 — an
  independent quantitative replication, conditional on the ratios
  conjecture (specarith/ph2r2/PH2R2_FINDINGS.md). Code is
  AGPL-3.0-or-later; llmspec results and write-ups are CC-BY-4.0
  (llmspec/LICENSE-RESULTS.md).
authors:
